This product bundles one engine sidecar, maleficium-engine, built by
scripts/build-engine.sh and packed into the installable next to the app
binary. It contains:

- Tectonic 0.17.0, built from its published source, MIT-licensed.
- latexml 0.7.6 (latexml-oxide), built from its published source, released
  under CC0 1.0; its dependencies carry their own licences (see the
  engine's Cargo.lock).
- The SyncTeX parser from jlaurens/synctex at commit
  04cf8e3e8665ff203248d7af78ee1129afbc1b64, vendored unmodified in
  src-tauri/engine/synctex under its MIT licence (Copyright Jerome Laurens
  2008-2024).

On Linux the installed engine binary also combines the following. Dynamic
entries link the host's shared libraries (they ship with the OS, pulled in
by the .deb Depends list, not copied into the binary); static entries are
compiled into the binary. Debian package names are as on Ubuntu 24.04, the
documented .deb build host:

- Tectonic 0.17.0's bridge crates (MIT) link dynamically: ICU
  (Unicode-DFS-2016 licence, Debian libicu74), freetype (FTL,
  libfreetype6), graphite2 (LGPL-2.1-or-later, also offered under
  MPL-1.1/GPL-2+, libgraphite2-3), fontconfig (MIT-style,
  libfontconfig1) and libpng (libpng licence, libpng16-16t64).
- HarfBuzz 8.3.0, compiled from the sources vendored in
  tectonic_bridge_harfbuzz (crate MIT) under HarfBuzz's Old MIT licence
  (Copyright 2010-2023 Google and others; full text in its COPYING),
  statically linked.
- libmarpa 8.6.2, compiled from the tarball vendored in libmarpa-asf-sys
  (crate MIT OR Apache-2.0) through the marpa-asf crate
  (MIT OR Apache-2.0), statically linked: marpa.c, marpa_ami.c and
  marpa_codes.c under the MIT licence (Copyright 2018 Jeffrey Kegler);
  marpa_obs.c and marpa_obs.h under LGPL-2.1-or-later (Copyright FSF, via
  the GNU C library); marpa_avl.c, marpa_tavl.c and their headers under
  LGPL-3-or-later. The vendored sources carry the full texts (COPYING for
  MIT, COPYING.LESSER for LGPL-3).
- libxml2 (MIT) and libxslt with libexslt (MIT), linked dynamically
  (libxml2, libxslt1.1) through the libxml and libxslt crates (MIT).
- zlib (zlib licence), compiled statically through libz-sys 1.1.29
  (crate MIT OR Apache-2.0) for the vendored SyncTeX parser above.

kpathsea is NOT in the Linux binary: with KPATHSEA_SKIP_TOOLCHAIN_CHECK=1
the kpathsea-sys build links nothing and latexml resolves files through
the engine's own kpsewhich stand-in (subprocess backend), so the LGPL-2.1
TeX Live C library is absent. The kpathsea and kpathsea-sys Rust crates
themselves are MIT OR Apache-2.0.

This product bundles, inlined into the built-in widget runtimes under
embed-runtime/built/ (built by `npm run build:runtimes`, no network at
build or run time), the Vega visualization stack and its dependencies, all
permissively licensed (checked against package-lock.json, 2026-10-01):

- vega 6.4.0, vega-lite 6.4.3 and vega-interpreter 2.3.2, Copyright (c)
  2015-present the Vega project and UW Interactive Data Lab, BSD-3-Clause.
- Their 76 transitive dependencies (d3-* and topojson-client under ISC or
  BSD-3-Clause; fast-deep-equal, json-stringify-pretty-compact and similar
  under MIT; tslib under 0BSD; robust-predicates under Unlicense).

The model runtime under embed-runtime/built/model/ also inlines three.js
0.186.1 (its GLTFLoader and OrbitControls included), Copyright (c) 2010-2026
three.js authors, MIT, with no dependencies (checked against package-lock.json,
2026-10-01). Its type declarations, @types/three 0.186.0 (MIT) and their
dependencies (MIT, Apache-2.0), are build-time only and not bundled. The video
runtime uses only the browser's own <video> element.

The model and video test fixtures under e2e/fixtures/ (a generated glb cube and
an ffmpeg test pattern, e2e/fixtures/gen-media.py) are original to Maleficium
and dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0.

This product bundles pdf.js (pdfjs-dist), Copyright Mozilla Foundation and
contributors, under the Apache License 2.0.

Its other npm and Rust dependencies keep their own licenses (MIT, ISC,
BSD-2/3-Clause, Apache-2.0, MPL-2.0, Zlib, Unicode-3.0, CC0 1.0 and similar),
and none is covered by Maleficium's AGPL-3.0 license. They are listed with
their versions in package-lock.json, src-tauri/Cargo.lock and
src-tauri/engine/Cargo.lock; each package's own license text is in its
published source. The Tectonic engine also builds in third-party C and C++
libraries (such as HarfBuzz, FreeType, ICU, libpng and zlib) under their own
licenses, documented in Tectonic's published source; the .deb links
libgraphite2 dynamically.

The built-in project templates under src-tauri/templates/ are original to
Maleficium and dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0
(src-tauri/templates/LICENSE); see src-tauri/templates/README.md.
